      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T19:15:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By \"original kernel\", do you mean Samsung\u0027s stock 4.4 kernel or the current 5.10 kernel?\n\nThe stock 4.4 headers match the 17-plane layout expected by the camera blob. In PS5, I didn\u0027t port the 4.4 headers. Instead, I selected the same 17-plane layout only for the ARM64 libhwjpeg in the 5.10 headers, while keeping the kernel\u0027s own ABI at 8 planes.\n\nIf you mean the current 5.10 headers, PS10 already uses them, but without the 17-plane selection, it ends up using 8 planes.\n\nI also tested this on the same ROM by changing only the ARM64 library. PS5 successfully saved photos, while PS10 caused the camera service to crash.",
      "parentUuid": "4ed0c7e3_daf1aeb2",
      "revId": "538c21985fe79773f20a497f89e76249feb5274b",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
    },
